{
  "rationale": "The plant automata model the robot's motion and perception capabilities, separating motion (G1) and perception (G2) for clarity and modularity. The specifications (E1-E4) bind perception outcomes to safe, progress-oriented actions, enforce conservative but non-repetitive recovery, and prevent unsafe or oscillatory behaviors. Recovery actions are short and directed, with full_rotate reserved for last-resort only after repeated failures. The design ensures forward progress dominates, with rapid return to exploration after recovery.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate plant automata for motion commands and perception outcomes to allow modular specification binding.",
    "Specification automata enforce safe, progress-maximizing action selection, conservative recovery, and prevent repeated or unsafe recovery actions."
  ],
